    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d480">

                <pb facs="0984" n="954" sameAs="frus:frus1947v01/pg954"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">560AL/6–1647: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Troutman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-06-16T16:00:00+01:00">June 16, 1947—2
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>509. Personal for Clayton from Wilcox. 1. Am being asked what is status of new
                    program for aid to Europe, whether it will be presented to ECE meeting and how
                    it is related to tariff and ITO negotiations.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d480-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>2. Contrast Bevin’s speech June 13 praising US offer of further aid with Cripps’
                    speech June 6<anchor n="2" xml:id="d480-f2"/> bitterly criticizing US and
                    disparaging importance tariff negotiations and ITO. Inference that aid program
                    makes results Geneva negotiations unimportant tends to impair our bargaining
                    position here. Question for consideration is how we can use program to improve
                    bargaining position.</p>
                <p>3. Assumption here has been that you will not return until wool issue settled. On
                    basis reports in press, am now being asked when you will return Geneva, whether
                    you will stop in London and Paris en route and what is schedule for subsequent
                    trips. [Wilcox.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Troutman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d480-f1" n="1" xml:id="d480-f1-content">
                <p>For documentation regarding the United States interest in the rehabilitation of
                    Europe and the “Marshall Plan,” see <ref target="frus1947v03#pg_197">Vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">iii</hi>, pp. 197</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d480-f2" n="2" xml:id="d480-f2-content">
                <p>The speech was given on June 11; see footnote 4, above.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
